ow  why and then he looks at another patient  of his named leonard played by robert de  niro who is the boy we saw at the  beginning the mother of this patient  explains to the doctor that her son does  not speak  but he communicates with her in other  ways although the doctor does not  understand how  that night the doctor has an idea and  returns to the hospital to further  investigate realizing that all those  patients fell into the state of lethargy  at the same year later the doctor sees a  girl playing hopscotch and he realizes  that his female patient did not continue  advancing in the room because there was  a cut in the checkered pattern floor and  when they fill it in they realize that  the patient manages to walk to a window  then the doctor investigates a life of  his other patient leonard  his mother explains that when he was a  child his condition gradually worsened  until he could no longer move or speak  he asked her what leonard liked and she  replies that he loved reading the next  day the doctor runs some studies on the  patient and shows the results to the  other doctors to whom he shows that  leonardo's brain reacted when he called  them by his name he continues to work  with the other patients when he gathers  together and teaches them to play ball  with each other another day he plays  opera music and the patient reacts to it  another nurse discovers that each  patient reacts to their favorite music  and thus more people join who help him  in his research one day the doctor uses  a ouija board to communicate with  leonard  at first he wants to teach him how to  spell but leonard selects the letters he  wants forming the title of a book that  the doctor later reads then he asks the  nurse about a drug used for parkinson's  patients a drug called aldoba  he investigates more about it with an  expert in this drug who tells him that  he is a chemist and he is a doctor so if  he wants to test that on his patients he  will be the one who should put 